# Every suite `make test` runs, in order. One command per line, relative to
# the repository root; the name in the report is the last word's basename.
#
# The list lives here rather than in the Makefile because tools/run-tests.sh
# has to be able to say "suite 11 of 22", and because a test can then drive
# the runner against a list of its own (test/test_run_tests.sh does).
# Every suite must end by printing one of the three verdict lines the runner
# reads: "ALL TESTS PASSED", "<n> FAILURES", or "<n> NOT MEASURED". A suite
# that exits without one has not been read, it has been interrupted, and the
# runner says so instead of guessing.

